  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "ITALIAN FAST LESSON IX"
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 2,
      "text": "CULTURAL NOTES"
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 3,
      "text": "TAXIS"
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 4,
      "text": "Italian taxis are distinguished by their color."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 5,
      "text": "In Rome, for example, they are yellow."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 6,
      "text": "The word TAXI appears on the side of the cab, and at times also on a luminous metal or plastic plate on the windshield."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 7,
      "text": "Taxis are found at special stands outside large hotels, railroad stations, airports, or in large squares or heavily-trafficked streets."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 8,
      "text": "If far from a taxi stand, you can call a cab after finding the number in the Yellow Pages (Pagine Gialle)."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 9,
      "text": "If you know the zone number of the nearest taxi stand, you can find the phone number listed by zone in the Yellow Pages."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 10,
      "text": "When a taxi has been called to pick someone up at a hotel or place of residence, the meter is activated the moment the driver leaves the taxi stand."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 11,
      "text": "By law, taxis must use the meter."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 12,
      "text": "A radio-taxi service also exists in some cities (see the telephone numbers in the Yellow Pages)."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 13,
      "text": "For long distances, such as between Rome and Fiumicino Airport or Milan and Malpensa Airport, it is better to take the airport buses that leave from the terminal, since taxi fares for these long rides are very high."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 14,
      "text": "Italian taxis add a surcharge for rides after 10:00 p.m., and also charge an additional fee for luggage."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 15,
      "text": "For rides outside the city limits, you must pay the driver a return fee."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 16,
      "text": "In Rome, taxi rates are posted in the passenger section in several languages."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 17,
      "text": "Taxi fares in Rome are relatively low, compared with other world capitals."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 18,
      "text": "A tip is customary."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 19,
      "text": "It is important to know that there are some people who have converted their cars into illegal taxicabs."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 20,
      "text": "Such drivers are commonly referred to as tassisti abusivi (\"abusive cabdrivers\")."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 21,
      "text": "They have no cab license and no meter in the car."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 22,
      "text": "It is best to avoid these \"cabs,\" since exorbitant fees may be charged for short rides."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 23,
      "text": "If you do take one, however, you should always ask for the price before getting into the car."
    }
  ],
